---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Admissions Pipeline Fix — Admissions & Referral Coordinator Toolkit"
  description="A complete system for admissions and referral coordinators at behavioral health and peer support programs. Intake workflows, referral tracking, follow-up scripts, and reporting tools."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-900 to-slate-900 text-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-20 sm:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <span class="inline-block bg-indigo-500/20 border border-indigo-400/30 text-indigo-300 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full mb-6">
          Session Supply Co. — Admissions & Referral Coordinator Toolkit
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight mb-6">Admissions Pipeline Fix</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Stop losing referrals in the inbox. This toolkit gives admissions and referral coordinators a real system — from first contact to enrolled client — so nothing falls through the cracks.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-400 mb-10">Built for behavioral health, peer support, and recovery programs that are growing faster than their intake process.</p>
        <a
          href="https://gumroad.com/l/PLACEHOLDER_ADMISSIONS_FIX"
          class="gumroad-button inline-block bg-indigo-500 hover:bg-indigo-400 text-white font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded-lg transition-colors text-lg"
          data-gumroad-overlay-checkout="true"
        >
          Get the Toolkit
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problem Section -->
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">A broken admissions process costs you more than empty beds</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Referral coordinators in behavioral health programs are often managing hundreds of open referrals across phone, fax, email, and EHR — with no unified system, no follow-up cadence, and no visibility into where things stand.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          The result: referrals go cold while the coordinator is playing phone tag. Funders ask for conversion data and there's no clean answer. Clinical staff gets frustrated when intake drops the ball on handoffs. And the coordinator is burned out and overwhelmed by a process that was never really designed.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          The Admissions Pipeline Fix is a complete operational system — not a lecture about the importance of follow-up, but the actual tools to do it differently starting this week.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What's Included -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 text-center mb-3">What's included</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-center mb-12 max-w-xl mx-auto">Every tool a referral coordinator needs to run a clean, traceable admissions pipeline.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {[
          {
            icon: 'M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2',
            title: 'Referral Tracking Spreadsheet',
            desc: 'A Google Sheets / Excel tracker covering every stage of the referral pipeline — source, status, follow-up date, barrier to admission, and outcome.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M8 7V3m8 4V3m-9 8h10M5 21h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 002 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z',
            title: 'Follow-Up Cadence Guide',
            desc: 'A day-by-day follow-up schedule for warm, cold, and pending referrals — with escalation triggers so nothing ages out without a decision.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M3 5a2 2 0 012-2h3.28a1 1 0 01.948.684l1.498 4.493a1 1 0 01-.502 1.21l-2.257 1.13a11.042 11.042 0 005.516 5.516l1.13-2.257a1 1 0 011.21-.502l4.493 1.498a1 1 0 01.684.949V19a2 2 0 01-2 2h-1C9.716 21 3 14.284 3 6V5z',
            title: 'Phone & Voicemail Scripts',
            desc: 'Word-for-word scripts for first outreach, follow-up calls, voicemails, and the "we haven\'t heard back" close — field-tested for behavioral health contexts.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z',
            title: 'Intake Workflow Map',
            desc: 'A step-by-step visual workflow from referral receipt to enrollment — including who owns each step, what gets documented, and where handoffs happen.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z',
            title: 'Referral Source Contact Log',
            desc: 'A system for managing relationships with referring providers — track contact history, communication preferences, and referral volume over time.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M9 19v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2zm0 0V9a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v10m-6 0a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v14a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2z',
            title: 'Monthly Pipeline Report Template',
            desc: 'A pre-built report template for presenting referral volume, conversion rates, and denial reasons to leadership and funders — no data wrangling required.',
          },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6">
            <div class="w-9 h-9 bg-indigo-50 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-indigo-700" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d={item.icon} />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who It's For -->
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Who this is for</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4">
            {[
              'Admissions coordinators managing referrals across multiple sources',
              'Referral coordinators at peer support, SUD, and mental health programs',
              'Program directors whose team is drowning in a broken intake process',
              'Organizations growing their census and needing to scale intake operations',
              'New coordinators who need a system to walk into, not build from scratch',
            ].map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-indigo-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                </svg>
                <span class="text-slate-700">{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-100 rounded-2xl p-8">
          <p class="text-indigo-900 font-semibold text-lg mb-3">Ready to fix your pipeline?</p>
          <p class="text-indigo-800 text-sm mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            One-time purchase, instant download. Every tool is ready to use out of the box — or customize for your program's specific workflow.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://gumroad.com/l/PLACEHOLDER_ADMISSIONS_FIX"
            class="gumroad-button inline-block w-full bg-indigo-700 hover:bg-indigo-800 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3.5 rounded-lg transition-colors text-center"
            data-gumroad-overlay-checkout="true"
          >
            Get the Toolkit
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 text-center mb-12">Common questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        {[
          {
            q: 'Does this work with our EHR?',
            a: 'The toolkit is EHR-agnostic — it\'s designed to work alongside whatever system you\'re using, not replace it. The tracking and reporting tools are in Sheets/Excel and Word/Docs so they plug into any workflow.',
          },
          {
            q: 'We have one coordinator managing everything. Is this still useful?',
            a: 'Yes — especially then. When one person owns the whole pipeline, having a clear system matters even more. The tools are sized for small teams and solo coordinators, not just large departments.',
          },
          {
            q: 'What format are the files?',
            a: 'Tracking tools are in Google Sheets and Excel. Scripts and workflow docs are in Word and Google Docs. All templates are fully editable.',
          },
          {
            q: 'We run a residential program. Will the intake workflow apply to us?',
            a: 'The workflow map includes common residential intake steps and can be customized for your level of care. The referral tracking and follow-up tools work across residential, outpatient, and community-based programs.',
          },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">{item.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.a}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
